            {
                "post_id": "post_94a5ecd8",
                "title": "Northern Range Wildlife Population Update — April 2026 Release",
                "body": "We are pleased to share the latest official wildlife population estimates for the Northern Range, drawn from the verified Q1 2026 survey datasets released on **2026-04-15** (v1.0) via FanaticWildlifeViews.com.\n\n**Gray Wolf (Canis lupus)**\n- Estimated population: **428 individuals**\n- Survey period: Q1 2026\n- Dataset: wds_gray_wolf_2026_04_15\n\n**Red Fox (Vulpes vulpes)**\n- Estimated population: **1,260 individuals**\n- Survey period: Q1 2026\n- Dataset: wds_red_fox_2026_04_15\n\nBoth datasets have been independently verified as the current approved release and cleared for publication. These figures reflect ongoing monitoring efforts across the Northern Range and will inform conservation planning for the remainder of 2026. Further updates will be posted as new survey data becomes available.",
                "published_at": "2026-11-01T23:52:51.727044Z",
                "channel": "conservation_blog"
            }
